dc75c2ae9" 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488385 1080 "(-\\frac{3}{2},-5)" 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488385 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488385 1083 #uuid "6ff2cc12-8660-5727-b18f-9ba7aed2ea2f" 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488386 1068 #edb/ref 17592186488388 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488386 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488386 1071 "![](images/a1/a1d3f3c077d921564732c5b27124a742f759e43dca9fb1cf9d8b931a24987dd0.png)\n\nFind the point on the line $y=-\\frac{2 x}{3} -5$ that is closest to the point $(2,-2).$" 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488386 1072 #uuid "749e94e9-2ffe-5773-8eda-37c34a18a98e" 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488386 1074 "First, we find the equation of the line that's perpendicular to $y=-\\frac{2 x}{3} -5$ and passes through the point $(2,-2).$\n\nThe given line has a slope of $-\\frac{2}{3},$ so our perpendicular line must have a slope of $\\frac{3}{2}.$\n\nUsing point-slope form and simplifying, we obtain the equation of the perpendicular line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-y_1 &= m(x-x_1) \\\\ y-(-2) &= \\frac{3}{2}(x-(2)) \\\\ y-(-2) &= \\frac{3 x}{2} -3 \\\\ y &= \\frac{3 x}{2} -5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now find the point where the two lines intersect. To do this, we solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{cases}y=-\\frac{2 x}{3} -5 \\\\ y=\\frac{3 x}{2} -5\\end{cases}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this system by putting the two equations equal to one another and solving for $x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2 x}{3} -5 &= \\frac{3 x}{2} -5 \\\\ -\\frac{13 x}{6} &= 0 \\\\ x &= 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=0$ into either of the two equations gives $y=-5.$ So, our solution is $x=0$ and $y=-5.$ Therefore, the lines intersect at the point $(0,-5).$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the point on the line $y=-\\frac{2 x}{3} -5$ that is closest to the point $(2,-2)$ is $(0,-5).$" 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488387 1080 "(3,-8)" 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488387 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488387 1083 #uuid "8d94a87b-0937-5a65-bad7-29f5651e091a" 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488388 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488381 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488388 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488383 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488388 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488384 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488388 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488390 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488388 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488391 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488388 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488388 1077 "selection" 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488388 1078 #edb/ref 17592186488384 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488388 1079 #uuid "a58e450a-0fc0-578a-adc5-f85b28ec0484" 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488389 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488379 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488389 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488380 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488389 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488382 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488389 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488385 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488389 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488387 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488389 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488389 1077 "selection" 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488389 1078 #edb/ref 17592186488379 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488389 1079 #uuid "ade496b6-83fd-5b55-8e55-9fbb16591fb4" 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488390 1080 "(3,-7)" 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488390 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535267 17592186045443 true] [17592186488390 1083 #uuid "bb0ff17a-224c-519e-bb32-5ca24c72a3